  "goodToKnow": "Der Lektor (die Lektorin) is an editor at a publishing house who selects and edits manuscripts: das Lektorat is the editorial department. At universities, a Lektor teaches a foreign language, often as a native speaker, for example through the DAAD. A newspaper or TV editor is der Redakteur. Lektorieren means to edit a text. Plural: die Lektoren, with stress moving to -to-."
